[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ Can you perform the main moves of the Stonewall Attack? }
1. d4 d5 2. e3 Nf6 3. Bd3 c5 { Whenever black plays c5 you must respond with c3 } { [%csl Gc3][%cal Gc2c3] } 4. c3 Nc6 { Where should this knight go? } { [%csl Gb1] } 5. Nd2 { Very well! } 5... Bg4 { On the main line the bishop was locked in his own pawn chain, but now the bishop is free.
What should you do now? } 6. Ngf3 { Excellent! Now we cover ourselves from the threat } 6... e6 { How do we attack the annoying bishop? } { [%csl Rg4] } 7. h3 { Very well! } { [%cal Rh3g4] } 7... Bh5 { How do we improve the king's situation? } 8. O-O { That's right!
Later, we can g4 and f4 to get the knight to e5 and continue with our plans. } { [%csl Ge5][%cal Gf3e5,Bf2f4,Bg2g4] } *

